0 This is the negative control for good-belt-on-pulleys.ldr, and it is a
0 real mistake, not an invented one. A D33 belt round two D24 pulleys
0 solves to a centre distance near 40 LDU. The seed rover's first draft
0 wrote that number straight into the design. A D24 pulley is 60 LDU
0 across, so at 40 apart the two overlap -- 304 LDU^3 here, and 1440 at
0 the 41 LDU the rover first used. The exact figure moves with how the
0 span lands on the voxel grid; that it is non-zero is the point.
    10|0
0 It exists so the four-stud span in the good fixture cannot quietly
0 revert to a number that only satisfies the belt.
